{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119137-protecting-your-sympathetic-name","id":1119137,"title":"Protecting your Sympathetic Name","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-21T18:51:42-07:00","id":1119137,"title":"Protecting your Sympathetic Name","content":"Mad Alice and Lewis Carol are cabal mates in a Wonderland themed Free Council cabal and they've been making trouble for a Seer of the Throne who goes by the name Lord Robert. After some detective work on everyone's part, they've each gotten a good look and/or pictures of each other. Given the availability of people lookup programs and stuff, is there anything any of them can do to protect their &quot;real&quot; identities at this point, or do mages need to be more proactive about differentiating their magical and civilian identities, using veiling magic and such?<br /> <br /> Or is there something built into the Shadow Name that prevents others from connecting the mage with her civilian identity without determined effort? Or do you need the Occultation merit for that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:03:28-07:00","id":1119166,"title":"","content":"Occultation and Shadow Name are the merits best suited to hiding your Sympathetic Name from another Mage since each has a specific level of protection it grants. Many Mages also engage in the use of the Alternate Identity merit which especially at the higher end can withstand some pretty thorough scrutiny, enough to mislead a potential foe.<br /> <br /> Even if your Sympathetic Name is discovered though, there are other defenses, such as Ward that you can employ to protect yourself from danger via Sympathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:22:34-07:00","id":1119176,"title":"","content":"But there's no inherent protection that I missed, right? Like, if a character would normally recognize a hostile Seer as Jim from I.T., they will, unless Jim has a spell or merit protecting their identity in some way (like the Jim identity being an Alternate that isn't their real name or a Mind spell that prevents anyone from recognizing you).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:31:45-07:00","id":1119180,"title":"","content":"Can't you also use Space to manipulate your sympathetic connection to your Shadow Name and/or other aspects of you (pictures of you, your appearance in general, where you live, etc.)?<br /> <br /> I assume weakening those connections would merely make it so anyone looking for you would have to double or triple check to make sure you're actually who they have pictures of. Like there is something off about you, but continued detective work would reinstate the connection.<br /> <br /> You could also combine it with a Mind spell, either replacing details of you with details of someone else or just memory holing them.<br /> <br /> One of the better solutions seems like Mind Wipe. Just make them forget they were ever investigating you and either take any evidence they have or force them to destroy it +amnesia while doing it.<br /> <br /> Ward seems like a safe bet if you don't want to be assaulted at range, but I don't know how helpful it is if they know where you live and you don't care to change your place of residence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">N/A</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11166-kryptonitekrusher","name":"kryptonitekrusher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-21T21:35:25-07:00","id":1119181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119137-protecting-your-sympathetic-name?p=1119176#post1119176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's no inherent protection that I missed, right? Like, if a character would normally recognize a hostile Seer as Jim from I.T., they will, unless Jim has a spell or merit protecting their identity in some way (like the Jim identity being an Alternate that isn't their real name or a Mind spell that prevents anyone from recognizing you).</div> </div> </div> </div>If Jim from I.T. hasn't invested in his Shadow Name enough to be at least a slightly different person when he's being a wizard, then no, he'll get no more protection against recognition than his mundane life's lack of complication from his Long-Term Nimbus. Putting more effort into his magical persona will throw off the scent, but that's the Merit in a nutshell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T01:03:21-07:00","id":1119203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119137-protecting-your-sympathetic-name#post1119137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mad Alice and Lewis Carol are cabal mates in a Wonderland themed Free Council cabal and they've been making trouble for a Seer of the Throne who goes by the name Lord Robert. After some detective work on everyone's part, they've each gotten a good look and/or pictures of each other. Given the availability of people lookup programs and stuff, is there anything any of them can do to protect their &quot;real&quot; identities at this point, or do mages need to be more proactive about differentiating their magical and civilian identities, using veiling magic and such?<br /> <br /> Or is there something built into the Shadow Name that prevents others from connecting the mage with her civilian identity without determined effort? Or do you need the Occultation merit for that?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not knowing names means one needs +1 potency on sympathetic spells or -2 dice, its not as big a deal as people seem to think it is. Remembering that multiple withstands just increase the biggest one by +1 each combining Shadow name and Occulation (4 to 6 merit points) wont always give good value. (Shadow Names yantra bonus is worth it though)<br /> <br /> <i>Occulation 1 means that your withstand varies between 3 and 5, (base occultation 1, + 1 strong connection, + 1 no name) vs (base weak connection 3 + occulation + no name)<br /> Occulation 3 means that your withstand varies between 5 and 5, (base occulation 3, + 1 strong connection, +1 no name) vs (base weak connection 3 + occulation + no name) -</i><b>Wrong..</b><br /> <br /> Shadow name will add another +1 on to this so you can get a base withstand of 6 vs sympathetic casting if you spend the full 6 merit points. (and keep your sympathetic name hidden). The person has to sink up to 12 dice into potency just to affect you.<br /> <br /> Remember exceptional successes can bypass the highest withstand also so your never 100% super safe anywhere or time. You'll want to get some spells that Clash vs what you think you might be up against too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 07-22-2017, 06:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T01:29:22-07:00","id":1119207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119137-protecting-your-sympathetic-name?p=1119203#post1119203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not knowing names means one needs +1 potency on sympathetic spells or -2 dice, its not as big a deal as people seem to think it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not being an insurmountable obstacle does not make it trivial; every Yantra dedicated to overcoming factor penalties is one you're not dedicating to actually increasing your dicepool (when you're already losing a slot just to use the Attainment), and pretty much every non-Yantra bonus is locked up in ritual casting time. Unless you're a Master of Space or intimately related to the target of your attentions, you have to Borrow or Perfect a sympathetic connection to mimic the mystical bond between them and their own flesh and blood; with how extensive the prep work can get, an extra level of Withstand is generally plenty significant for a mage looking to mess with a rival from afar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remembering that multiple withstands just increase the biggest one by +1 each combining Shadow name and Occulation (4 to 6 merit points) wont always give good value. (Shadow Names yantra bonus is worth it though) </div> </div> </div>You don't combine Occultation and Shadow Name for the Withstand boosts alone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (base occultation 1, + 1 strong connection, + 1 no name) </div> </div> </div>Occultation doesn't give you an extra Withstand on top of the one your connection already merits. Also, Connected sympathy is still part of the range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-22T03:33:25-07:00","id":1119216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1119137-protecting-your-sympathetic-name?p=1119207#post1119207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not being an insurmountable obstacle does not make it trivial; every Yantra dedicated to overcoming factor penalties is one you're not dedicating to actually increasing your dicepool (when you're already losing a slot just to use the Attainment), and pretty much every non-Yantra bonus is locked up in ritual casting time. Unless you're a Master of Space or intimately related to the target of your attentions, you have to Borrow or Perfect a sympathetic connection to mimic the mystical bond between them and their own flesh and blood; with how extensive the prep work can get, an extra level of Withstand is generally plenty significant for a mage looking to mess with a rival from afar.<br /> <br /> You don't combine Occultation and Shadow Name for the Withstand boosts alone.<br /> <br /> Occultation doesn't give you an extra Withstand on top of the one your connection already merits. Also, Connected sympathy is still part of the range.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm yeh Occultation just sets the min level of the connection withstand? Suppose it helps vs people borrowing strong connections or increasing them with web-weaver, if its always 3 like a weak connection. <br /> <br /> The point is people seem to think if somebody finds out their sympathetic name then they are doomed, when in fact its only slightly easier for somebody to cast on them. Sure try to keep it a secret but dont freak out if somebody finds it. Also spending to much time and effort trying to keep it secret might not be worth the effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}